// Where a waterfall lands, in layers: mist boiling up and rolling away, a low bank of it lying
// on the pool, crowns of white water where the ropes hit, drops thrown out, and rings of foam
// spreading on the surface. Written for a fall about 5 meters wide; the land scales it by the
// fall's width (see `add_fresh_water`). Everything ends by fading and thinning, never at once.
